{"abstract":[{"text":"In Godot, class members can be exported. This means their value gets saved along","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the resource (such as the scene) they’re attached to. They will also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available for editing in the property editor. Exporting is done by using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Export","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" annotation.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Exports"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Articles-and-Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Differences","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variants","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RemoteProcedureCalls","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BindingNodes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RunningInEditor","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MemoryManagement","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypesTranslation","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Documentation"],"title":"Articles and Tutorials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This document deals with exporting properties, for information about exposing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functions to the Godot world, see the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","isActive":true},{"text":" document.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Introduction to Exports","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Introduction-to-Exports"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way of exporting a variable is to annotate it with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Export","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute, like this:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiftGodot","","@Godot","public class ExportExample: Node3D","{","    @Export","    var number = 5","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In that example the value 5 will be saved, and after building the current","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project it will be visible in the property editor.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One of the fundamental benefits of exporting member variables is to have them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visible and editable in the editor. This way, artists and game designers can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modify values that later influence how the program runs. For this, a special export syntax is provided.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Export"},{"type":"text","text":" can be applied to non-static, non-class variables with following types:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantConvertible"},{"text":" types and their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Optional"},{"text":"s such as:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1.1. Swift primitive types (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float"},{"type":"text","text":", any width signed and unsigned version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":" (such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1.2. All builtin Godot types present in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantArray"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vector3"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Callable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Signal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1.3. All "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Object"},{"type":"text","text":"-derived types including your own types."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1.4. Your custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":" types."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any Swift closures taking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments and returning "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Void"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":" value without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" specifier."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CaseIterable"},{"type":"text","text":" enum having integer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RawValue"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Export"},{"type":"text","text":" macro only works in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Godot"},{"type":"text","text":" class declaration, and will not work on Swift class extensions."}]},{"code":["\/\/ Correct","@Godot","class YourClass {","    @Export var int = 42","}","","\/\/ Incorrect","extension YourClass {","    @Export var anotherInt = 48","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Basic Usage","anchor":"Basic-Usage","type":"heading","level":3},{"code":["@Export","var number: Int","","@Export","var anotherNumber { get { ... } set { ... } }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exported members can specify a default value:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var number: Int = 0","","@Export","var text: String? = nil        \/\/ Allows for nil","","@Export","var greeting = \"Hello World\"   \/\/ Exported field specifies a default value"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Resources and nodes can be exported."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","public var resource: Resource { ","    get { ","        return myInternalResource","    } ","    set { ","        print (\"Setting my resource\")","    } ","}","","@Export","public var node: Node { ","    get { ","        return myInternalNode","    } ","    set { ","        print (\"Setting the node\")","    } ","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Grouping Exports","anchor":"Grouping-Exports","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is possible to group your exported properties inside the Godot Inspector with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the #exportGroup macro. Every exported property after this annotation will be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"added to the group.  Start a new group or use #export_group (””) to break out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#exportGroup(\"My Properties\")","@Export var number = 3"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also specifiy that only properties with a given prefix be grouped, like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["#exportGroup(\"My Properties\", prefix: \"health\")","@Export var health_reload_speed = 3"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Groups cannot be nested, use #exportSubgroup to create subgroups within a group.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["#exportSubgroup(\"Extra Properties\")","#export var string = \"\"","#export var flag = false"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Customizing-the-Exported-Value","text":"Customizing the Exported Value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can pass a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyHint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter to the Export attribute, along with additional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data to control how the property is surfaced in the editor.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, to surface the property as a file and trigger the file selector in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UI, use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".file"},{"type":"text","text":" value:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.file)","var GameFile: String? "],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String as a path to a directory."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.dir)","var gameDirectory: String?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String as a path to a file, custom filter provided as hint."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export (.file, \"*.txt\")","var GameFile: String?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Using paths in the global filesystem is also possible, but only in scripts in tool mode.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String as a path to a PNG file in the global filesystem."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export (.globalFile, \"*.png\")","var toolImage: String?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"String as a path to a directory in the global filesystem.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export (.globalDir)","var toolDir: String?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The multiline annotation tells the editor to show a large input field for editing over multiple lines."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export (.multilineText)","var text: String?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Limiting-editor-input-ranges","text":"Limiting editor input ranges","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using the range property hint allows you to limit what can be input as a value using the editor."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Allow integer values from 0 to 20."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.range, \"0,20,\")","var number: Int = 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Allow integer values from -10 to 20."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.range, \"-10,20,\")","var number: Int =  0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Allow floats from -10 to 20 and snap the value to multiples of 0.2.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.range, \"-10,20,0.2\")","var number = 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you add the hints "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"or_greater"},{"type":"text","text":" and\/or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"or_less"},{"type":"text","text":" you can go above or below the limits when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adjusting the value by typing it instead of using the slider."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.range, \"0,100,1,or_greater,or_less\")","var number: Int = 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Floats-with-easing-hint","text":"Floats with easing hint","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Display a visual representation of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ease()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function when editing.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Export(.expEasing)","public transitionSpeed: Float = 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Colors","text":"Colors","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Regular color given as red-green-blue-alpha value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var color: Color { get {} set {} }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Color given as red-green-blue value (alpha will always be 1)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export(.colorNoAlpha)","var color: Color { get {} set {} }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Nodes","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Nodes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since Godot 4.0, nodes can be directly exported without having to use NodePaths."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","public Node node { get; set; }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom node classes can also be used, see C# global classes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exporting NodePaths like in Godot 3.x is still possible, in case you need it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var nodePath: NodePath","","public override func _ready() ","{","    var node = GetNode(nodePath)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Node","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type will have their ","type":"text"},{"code":".nodeType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically filled, so that Editor will allow","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Camera3D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" subtypes to be set to the following exported property:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export \/\/ no need to write @Export(.nodeType, \"Camera3D\")","var camera: Camera3D? = nil"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Resources","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Resources"},{"code":["@Export","var resource: Resource { get {} set {} }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the Inspector, you can then drag and drop a resource file from the FileSystem dock into the variable slot."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opening the inspector dropdown may result in an extremely long list of possible classes to create, however."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Therefore, if you specify a type derived from Resource such as:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var resource: AnimationNode"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The drop-down menu will be limited to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AnimationNode","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and all its inherited classes."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Custom resource classes can also be used, see Swift global classes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must be noted that even if the script is not being run while in the editor, the exported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties are still editable. This can be used in conjunction with a script in “tool” mode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Arrays","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Arrays"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To surface arrays in Godot, use a strong type for it, for example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var myResources: TypedArray<Vector3>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Alternatively, if you want to surface an array of Godot objects, or even your own subclasses of those, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"TypedArray<YourCustomType?>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", for example:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Export","var myNodes: TypedArray<MySpinnerCube?>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"⚠️ Note ⚠️","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"%E2%9A%A0%EF%B8%8F-Note-%E2%9A%A0%EF%B8%8F"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Object","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" derived types require optional "},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That’s due to Godot absence of guarantee that that "},{"code":"Array[Object]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t contain "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Enumeration Values","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Enumeration-Values"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To surface enumeration values, you need to use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CaseIterable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RawValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryInteger","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum MyEnum: Int, CaseIterable {","    case first","    case second","}","","@Godot","class Sample: Node {","    @Export \/\/ no need to use @Export(.enum), it will be filled automatically","    var myValue: MyEnum","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Exports","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/exports"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/RemoteProcedureCalls":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RemoteProcedureCalls","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/remoteprocedurecalls","title":"Remote Procedure Calls","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Rpc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro to configure methods for Godot’s multiplayer RPC system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/TypesTranslation":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/typestranslation","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Types Translation","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypesTranslation","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This document contains information on how type translation happens between Swift and Godot."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Camera3D":{"abstract":[{"text":"Camera node, displays from a point of view.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Camera3D","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/camera3d","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Camera3D","type":"topic","title":"Camera3D","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Camera3D","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/BindingNodes":{"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BindingNodes","kind":"article","title":"Referencing Nodes from your Scene","abstract":[{"text":"You will find yourself referencing nodes from a scene in your code. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"GDScript, that is usually achieved by using the dollar sign and the name of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object you want to reference.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/bindingnodes"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/RunningInEditor":{"type":"topic","title":"Running Code in the Godot Editor","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RunningInEditor","abstract":[{"text":"There are cases where you might want some of your Swift code for your extension","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to run while it is being used in the Godot Editor.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/runningineditor","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/AnimationNode":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AnimationNode"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AnimationNode"}],"title":"AnimationNode","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/animationnode","abstract":[{"text":"Base class for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AnimationTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" nodes. Not related to scene nodes.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AnimationNode"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Documentation":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/documentation","kind":"article","title":"Documenting your Godot Extension","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are developing a Godot extension that is intended to be consumed from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Godot you might want to provide documentation for it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Documentation","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CustomTypes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/customtypes","title":"Using Custom Types","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"You will typically extend the functionality of your Godot game by creating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"classes that derive from one of the various Godot types and adjust the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behavior accordingly."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Variants":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/variants","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variants","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Variants","abstract":[{"text":"Follow up on the fundamental building block of Godot’s data types.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/AnimationTree":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AnimationTree","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AnimationTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A node used for advanced animation transitions in an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AnimationPlayer"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/animationtree","title":"AnimationTree","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/AnimationTree","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Signals":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/signals","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Signals","abstract":[{"text":"Signals in Godot are used by objects to post interesting events that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taking place, and can be used by users to easily add behavior and react","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to changes.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/MemoryManagement":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/memorymanagement","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MemoryManagement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftGodot surfaces various Godot types into the Swift universe in various ways:"}],"title":"Memory Management in SwiftGodot","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Differences":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/differences","kind":"article","title":"SwiftGodot API differences to GDScript","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This document lists some common differences between GDSscript and SwiftGodot."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Differences"}}}